WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.334
-Thank you so much.
You look gorgeous.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.601
So --
-Look, it's people.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.701
-I know. There's people here!
isn't that great?!

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.133
-Hi!
-I know. It's the best.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thanks for being here in studio.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.767
-I am so happy to be here.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.367
-It means a lot to us,
so thank you.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:16.067
We've crossed paths, but we've
never actually met before.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.467
-Yeah.
I've seen from you afar a lot.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.467
-Yeah.
-And I'm always like, "Hi."

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.667
Because we have friends
in common, which, for me,

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.734
it's like third-degree
separation.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:25.934
-Yeah.
-Like...

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.567
your favorite person ever,
Justin Timberlake,

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.534
who I worked with
and did a music video --

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.100
I was like,
"Okay, so, I know Justin,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.801
so now I'm friends with Jimmy."
-Yeah.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:34.868
-Because --
-Of course.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.200
-It's like --
-Yeah. We're besties now.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.400
-We're best friends.
I'm your favorite new Aquarius.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.801
-Yeah, I will take that.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.634
Yeah, I love that.
[ Applause ]

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:42.968
What was your plan?

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.601
'Cause I know you were
a big star in Latin America.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:47.367
But did you plan on just coming
to the States and taking over?

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.767
-No. Never.
That was never a plan at all.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:52.267
I was actually
just swinging by L.A.,

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:55.534
and I was just,
for random reasons, there.

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:56.801
And I rented --
this, like, lady --

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.067
before Airbnb existed,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.100
like, an old lady's house
in the back,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.767
and I was just staying there
and depressed.

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.501
And my mom was like, "Why
don't you go to an audition?"

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.801
I'm like,
"Mom, that's not how it works."

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.667
Like, I'm --
Imagine, if it was like --

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.868
Yeah,
I just to go to an audition,

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.801
become a Hollywood star.
It's, like, very hard.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:12.834
I was like, "Yes, Mom."

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:13.901
She's like, "Oh, my God.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.501
I heard about this thing
called IMDbPro.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.801
I'm gonna sign you up.
It's fine."

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.033
I was like, "Sure, Mom."
So then, sure enough,

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:22.300
my mother sort of found a way
to get me an audition.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.801
-See?
-And I go to this audition.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:26.000
And I was terrified,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.234
'cause English is
my second language,

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.000
and I was like --
never done this before.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.334
So I, like, did it,
and I did another audition

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:32.968
and clearly didn't get it,

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.767
and then found out
it was "Star Wars."

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.767
It was "The Force Awakens."
-Wow.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.367
-And I had no idea.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:41.634
But, then, I just moved back.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.968
And then, at the time,
I had bought --

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.067
I don't know if you remember.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:47.434
This was like 2007,
you guys, '08 --

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:50.501
where you have to
buy a flip phone at the 7-Eleven

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.167
'cause you couldn't get, like,
a phone on the store

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.667
if you were, like, from Mexico.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.334
You needed, like, a -- all the
shebangs of being an American.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.434
So I had this flip phone,

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.234
'cause I was texting
with this guy.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:03.734
So that was the one thing
I got in L.A. -- had a hot boy.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.834
So, I was in a bridal shoot.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.067
This is wild.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.234
-I was in the middle
of a bridal shoot

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:12.033
and, you know, big, big dresses,
just like today.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.701
And I'm sitting there, and I
get a phone call, and I pick up.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.334
And they're like,
"Is this Eiza González?"

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.801
I'm like, "Yeah. Who is this?"
"Mary Vernieu."

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.000
And I'm like,
"I don't know who you are."

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.300
-Mary Vernieu?

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.501
-She's a huge casting director
in Hollywood.

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:23.634
-Amazing, yeah.
-Massive.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:24.701
-Legend.
-She's like,

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:25.901
"Can you tape yourself
right now?

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:26.934
I need it now."

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.801
And I'm like,
"I'm in a bridal shoot."

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.467
So I, like, took off my dress.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.033
I have a dress on the bottom
like this big,

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.167
and I have a shirt.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.400
And I taped against a wall
with a page.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.000
And -- And, yeah,
then they called me.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.067
They're like, "Can you fly in?

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.868
Robert Rodriguez
wants to meet you."

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.234
I was like, "Okay."

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.901
And then, the next day,
I was moving to Austin, Texas,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.300
and I booked my first show.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.901
Got the show,
didn't get the guy.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.167
But, you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.501
-Hey, no, I mean --
But look at you now, right?

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:50.601
Come on.
-Hi!

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:51.701
-In the number-one movie
in the country.

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:52.801
-He should have texted me back.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.167
You should've texted her back,
buddy.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.167
She's in the number-one movie.
Come on. Yeah, exactly.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.868
Let's talk about
"Godzilla vs. Kong."

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.634
-Yes.
-It is massive.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.634
-Yeah.
-Globally massive.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.367
How is it like to act
where there's like --

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:07.634
there's nothing
really real, right?

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.267
-Yeah, yeah.
Nothing's real.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.801
Sorry, guys.
Godzilla does not exist.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.767
Or Kong. I mean, he does --
in our imaginations.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.968
-Yeah.
-But I was just terrified,

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.667
because, you know,
when you're doing these movies,

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:18.934
you don't really know
what you're gonna do.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.067
And one of the first things
that happened to me

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:25.000
that I realized on the day
was that I have motion sickness.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.300
-So, we were on set and, yeah,
I was in a thing called "HEAV."

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.968
And they strap you into it.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:35.701
And I had four words to say --
no joke, guys -- four words.

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:36.634
And I'm like --

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.400
[ Retching ]
-No.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.767
And then I'm like --
[ Retching ]

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.000
And then,
it was my birthday that day.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.000
And the director's like,
"It's fine. You can do it."

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.334
I'm like, "Sure, sure."
And I'm nervous.

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.534
English is my second language.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.701
I'm like, "I can do this.
This is five words.

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.033
I can do this."

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.567
Um, I couldn't.

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:52.968
I almost threw up.

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:54.567
It was my birthday,
and they're like, "Great.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.767
We're gonna cut this scene
out of the movie,

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:56.901
but, come --
happy birthday!"

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.300
♪ Happy birthday ♪

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.801
And they pull like five cakes,
and I'm like...

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.100
[ Both retching ]
-I'm like...

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.767
-Like, "Don't
take the cake out of it."

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.334
What -- it's called the HEAV?

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.067
-It's a HEAV, yeah,
in the movie --

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.634
you have to watch the movie
to know what it is.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.234
-Yeah. Did you get a chance
to see it in the theater or...?

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.400
-I did.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.734
I watched it in a movie theater
by myself,

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:17.067
which is really exciting
because I'm that type of person

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.167
that likes to be very mindful
when I'm in the movie theater.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.300
I don't talk.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.300
And I was like, "Whoa! Wow!"
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.634
-"I'm alone!
I can scream."

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.834
I was just screaming
the whole time.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.501
It is just definitely
a "pinch me" moment

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.067
when you're part
of those massive movies

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.501
and you have no idea
how it's gonna look like.

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.167
I did, however,
leaving the movie

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.934
wish I would have done it
on shrooms.

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:38.067
I was like, "This is wild."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.100
I need to do it all over again.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:42.767
-Okay, alright...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.000
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.834
Here's Eiza González
in "Godzilla vs. Kong."

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.200
Take a look.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.000
[ Kong growls softly ]

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.701
-Wow. Who's the idiot
who came up with this idea?

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.501
[ Kong snarls ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:58.033
-I'm Maia Simmons.
My father sent me.

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.534
I run point for Apex.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:00.734
-Nathan Lind, mission chief.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.167
[ Kong roaring ]

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.601
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:04.968
-Yeah, don't worry.

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:06.501
I'm just here to babysit.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.434
[ Kong roaring ]
[ Metal clanging ]

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:09.801
The Hollow Earth Aerial Vehicles

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:12.367
are on their way to Antarctica
as we speak.

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:14.667
I know you people think
you're cutting-edge,

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.067
but these prototypes
we're loaning you

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:19.834
will make what you've been
flying look like used Miatas.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.234
-I love Miatas.
[ Kong growling ]

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:23.601
-Forget about the price tag,
which is obscene, of course.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.767
The antigravity engines alone
produce enough charge

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:27.033
to light up Vegas for a week.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.501
[ Kong roars ]

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.567
-All members on the main deck.
-Feel free to be impressed.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:31.667
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.667
Feel free to be impressed.
-Seriously.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.167
-Eiza González, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:36.767
"Godzilla vs. Kong"

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:39.634
is in theaters
and streaming on HBO Max now.

